    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2024-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write \\(10! = 10 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7! = 720 \\cdot 7!.\\) But \\(720 = 6!\\) too, so \\(10! = 6! \\cdot 7! = 7! \\cdot 6!.\\) The two terms are the same. That makes \\(10! - 7! \\cdot 6! = 0.\\) Therefore, the answer is B.",
